  "latency_total_seconds": 252.217,
  "prompt": "/deep-research According to the ACT, for 2023 identify of all the states to have an estimated at least 90% of their grads tested using the ACT, which of those states had a composite average score of at least 18.5, had at least 42% of test takers meet the English benchmark, had at least 19% meet the math benchmark, and at least 30% meet the reading benchmark.",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "According to the ACT, for 2023 identify of all the states to have an estimated at least 90% of their grads tested using the ACT, which of those states had a composite average score of at least 18.5, had at least 42% of test takers meet the English benchmark, had at least 19% meet the math benchmark, and at least 30% meet the reading benchmark.",
  "answer": "Based on the official ACT 2023 \"Average ACT Scores by State\" report and NCES Digest Table 226.60, I've analyzed all 50 states + DC against your five criteria.\n\n## States Meeting All Five Criteria (7 states)\n\n| State | % Tested | Composite | % English (≥18) | % Math (≥22) | % Reading (≥22) |\n|-------|----------|-----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| Arkansas | 96% | 18.6 | 48% | 21% | 33% |\n| Kentucky | 100% | 18.7 | 49% | 23% | 36% |\n| Montana | 98% | 18.8 | 44% | 26% | 36% |\n| Nebraska | 96% | 19.2 | 50% | 29% | 36% |\n| Utah | 90% | 19.9 | 55% | 32% | 44% |\n| Wisconsin | 95% | 19.4 | 51% | 31% | 38% |\n| Wyoming | 100% | 19.0 | 48% | 25% | 37% |\n\n## Verification Against Each Criterion\n\n1. **≥90% graduates tested**: All 7 states meet this (90–100%)\n2. **Composite ≥18.5**: All 7 states meet this (18.6–19.9)\n3. **≥42% English benchmark**: All 7 states meet this (44–55%)\n4. **≥19% Math benchmark**: All 7 states meet this (21–32%)\n5. **≥30% Reading benchmark**: All 7 states meet this (33–44%)\n\n## States That Fell Short (tested ≥90% but failed other criteria)\n\n| State | Failed Criterion(s) |\n|-------|---------------------|\n| Alabama | Composite 18.0 (<18.5) |\n| Arizona | Composite 17.7 (<18.5) |\n| Louisiana | Composite 18.2 (<18.5) |\n| Mississippi | Composite 17.6 (<18.5) |\n| Nevada | Composite 17.2 (<18.5) |\n| North Carolina | English 41% (<42%) |\n| Oklahoma | Composite 17.8 (<18.5) |\n| Tennessee | Composite 18.4 (<18.5) |\n\n**Note**: North Dakota (89% tested) and Ohio (82% tested) did not meet the ≥90% participation threshold.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. **ACT 2023 State Data PDF** — Complete table with participation rates, composite scores, and benchmark percentages for all 50 states + DC  \n   https://www.act.org/content/dam/act/secured/documents/2023-Average-ACT-Scores-by-State.pdf\n\n2. **NCES Digest Table 226.60** — Participation rates and subject-area scores (Excel download)  \n   https://nces.ed.gov/programs/digest/d23/tables/dt23_226.60.asp\n\n3. **ACT 2023 National Profile Report** — Confirms benchmark definitions: English=18, Math=22, Reading=22, Science=23  \n   https://www.act.org/content/dam/act/unsecured/documents/2023-National-ACT-Profile-Report.pdf\n\n**Benchmark interpretation**: \"% meeting benchmark\" means students scoring at or above the ACT College Readiness Benchmark scores (English ≥18, Math ≥22, Reading ≥22).",
  "answer_chars": 2374,
  "expected_answer": "Kentucky, Wyoming, Montana, Arkansas, Nebraska, Wisconsin, Utah",
